hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17950","Affan narrated to us, he said, Shubah narrated to us, he said, Abu Bakr ibn Hafs said, he informed me, he said, I heard Abu Musabbih, or Ibn Musabbih, Abu Bakr doubted, from Ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Abd Allah ibn Rawahah. He said, So he did not move aside for him from his bed, and said, Do you know who are the martyrs of my nation. They said, A Muslim being killed is martyrdom. He said, The martyrs of my nation are then few. A Muslim being killed is martyrdom, and plague is martyrdom, and the woman whom her child kills while dying in childbed."
